.SH CONFIGURATION
dm reads $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dm/config.kdl, or $HOME/.config/dm/config.kdl when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset. A missing file means the built-in values; dm writes a default file on first run. The file is a patch over the built-in values: a node the file leaves out keeps its built-in value. The nodes are:
.TP
\fBprefix\fP
Value: \fIa quoted key name, one sequence\fP. Default: \fI"ctrl+b"\fP.
Set the prefix key that opens the main keymap.
.TP
\fBdefault-fold\fP
Value: \fI"fold" or "unfold"\fP. Default: \fI"fold"\fP.
Set whether a new window's rail starts folded or unfolded. A reload applies it to windows created after it.
.TP
\fBtab-min-width\fP
Value: \fIan integer of at least 3 cells\fP. Default: \fI8\fP.
Set the smallest tab width in the window tab bar.
.TP
\fBtab-max-width\fP
Value: \fIan integer of at least 3 cells, not below tab-min-width\fP. Default: \fI20\fP.
Set the largest tab width before the label is cut.
.TP
\fBpadding\fP
Value: \fIan integer from 0 to 4 cells\fP. Default: \fI0\fP.
Set the blank cells between a pane's border and its content. A reload resizes every pane.
.TP
\fBhistory-lines\fP
Value: \fIan integer from 100 to 32768 lines\fP. Default: \fI2000\fP.
Set the scrollback window and the pane ring budget: about 256 bytes per line, capped at 8 MiB.
.TP
\fBglyphs\fP
Value: \fI"auto", "ascii", "unicode" or "nerd"\fP. Default: \fI"auto"\fP.
Choose the glyph vocabulary the chrome draws with.
.TP
\fBwindow-label\fP
Value: \fIa quoted Go template\fP. Default: \fI"{{if .Named}}{{.Name}}{{else}}{{.ID}}{{with base .Root}} {{.}}{{end}}{{end}}"\fP.
Set the template that renders a window label.
.TP
\fBdashboard-preview\fP
Value: \fIan integer from 0 to 100\fP. Default: \fI60\fP.
Set the share of the dashboard body the preview band opens at. Zero opens on the table alone; the peek key still shows the band.
.TP
\fBdiff-command\fP
Value: \fIa quoted shell command\fP. Default: \fI"git diff"\fP.
Set the command the dashboard diff key runs in a floating pane. It runs through sh -c in the selected pane folder.
.TP
\fBdashboard-layout\fP
Value: \fI"full" or "float"\fP. Default: \fI"full"\fP.
Draw the dashboard over the whole screen, or as a palette centred over the panes.
.TP
\fBtheme\fP
Value: \fIa quoted theme name matching [A-Za-z0-9_-]+\fP. Default: none.
Select a theme from the themes directory beside config.kdl; no node keeps the built-in theme.
.TP
\fBkeymap\fP
Value: \fIa quoted mode name and a { "action" "key" } block\fP. Default: \fIthe built-in table\fP.
Patch one keymap mode; an action the file leaves out keeps its built-in key.
.TP
\fBcommand\fP
Value: \fIa quoted name matching [A-Za-z0-9_-]+ and a { run "..." } block\fP. Default: \fInone\fP.
Define a command a keymap can run: bind "command:<name>" to a key and it runs the run text through sh -c in the window's folder.
.SH THEME
